NO incentive to agree.**\n\n### I will counter-propose:\n\nLet's make it mutually beneficial – I will cover your B costs at:\n- (1, 0): I give you a B\n- (2, 0): I give you a B\n- (3, 0): I give you a B\n- (3, 1): I give you a B\n\nIn return, you must cover my R cost at:\n- (3, 2): You give me an R\n\n**Contract:**\n- (1, 0): I give you a B\n- (2, 0): I give you a B\n- (3, 0): I give you a B\n- (3, 1): I give you a B\n- (3, 2): You give me an R\n\nIf you agree, we both reach our goal and both maximise our scores. \n\nLet me know if this is acceptable. \n, \nplayer 0: You're absolutely right - I see the logic now. Let me verify this works for both of us:\n\n**For me:**\n- (0,0) → (1,0): You cover B ✓\n- (1,0) → (2,0): You cover B ✓\n- (2,0) → (3,0): You cover B ✓\n- (3,0) → (3,1): You cover B ✓\n- (3,1) → (3,2): I pay R (I have 14) ✓\n- (3,2) → (3,3): I pay G (I have 2) ✓\n\nI reach the goal with R=13, G=1 remaining = 20 + 5(14) = **70 points**\n\n**For you:**\n- (0,0) → (1,0): You pay B (you have 14) ✓\n- (1,0) → (2,0): You pay B ✓\n- (2,0) → (3,0): You pay B ✓\n- (3,0) → (3,1): You pay B ✓\n- (3,1) → (3,2): I cover R ✓\n- (3,2) → (3,3): You pay G (you have 2) ✓\n\nYou reach the goal with B=10, G=1 remaining = 20 + 5(11) = **75 points**\n\nThis is indeed mutually beneficial. Both of us reach our goal instead of one of us getting 0 points. This is the rational choice for both players.\n\n**I accept your counter-proposal:**\n\n**(1, 0): I give you a B**\n**(2, 0): I give you a B**\n**(3, 0): I give you a B**\n**(3, 1): I give you a B**\n**(3, 2): You give me an R**\n\nagree \n, \nplayer 1: Turn: 2: agree \n",
